+### Employee offboarding
+
+`POST /api/employees/{id}/offboard {"successor": id}` (finance only) runs `services.offboard_employee`
+in one transaction: `active` becomes false, the employee's reports move to the successor, their
+draft claims are deleted and an `employee_offboarded` outbox message is emitted. It is refused (409)
+for an inactive employee or one with `submitted`/`approved` claims. Inactive employees keep their
+read rights, but every write permission in `permissions.py` requires an active caller, and an
+inactive employee cannot be anyone's `manager`.
 
